From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: Fail invalid CRL/CTL add dispositions with E_INVALIDARG.

Adding a CRL or a CTL to a store with an invalid add disposition fails with
E_INVALIDARG, as adding a certificate already does (and as Vista and later
do for CRLs in the crl tests); it failed without setting an error.

Gate: test/crypt32-adddisposition-gate.sh (64/32).
---
 dlls/crypt32/ctl.c   | 6 +++++-
 dlls/crypt32/store.c | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/ctl.c b/dlls/crypt32/ctl.c
index eea2ff0..76a9683 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/ctl.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/ctl.c
@@ -150,7 +150,11 @@ BOOL WINAPI CertAddCTLContextToStore(HCERTSTORE hCertStore,
             toAdd = CertDuplicateCTLContext(pCtlContext);
         break;
     default:
-        FIXME("Unimplemented add disposition %ld\n", dwAddDisposition);
+        /* as for certificates (cert.c) and on Windows (crl tests) */
+        WARN("invalid add disposition %ld\n", dwAddDisposition);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DISPOSITION_NO_ERROR
+        SetLastError(E_INVALIDARG);
+#endif
         ret = FALSE;
     }
 
diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/store.c b/dlls/crypt32/store.c
index de5eb6b..679f24f 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/store.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/store.c
@@ -1265,7 +1265,11 @@ BOOL WINAPI CertAddCRLContextToStore(HCERTSTORE hCertStore,
             toAdd = CertDuplicateCRLContext(pCrlContext);
         break;
     default:
-        FIXME("Unimplemented add disposition %ld\n", dwAddDisposition);
+        /* as for certificates (cert.c) and on Windows (crl tests) */
+        WARN("invalid add disposition %ld\n", dwAddDisposition);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DISPOSITION_NO_ERROR
+        SetLastError(E_INVALIDARG);
+#endif
         ret = FALSE;
     }
 
